course: dictionary
lesson: 3198
title: Words for energy and action
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Energetic describes someone or something that has lots of energy. An energetic person or animal is active and lively, and an energetic activity needs a lot of effort, like running or dancing. Look for clues in the words around it.
explain: «Big, energetic dogs like huskies need lots of space and hours of running every day.» The clues are lots of space and hours of running, so energetic means full of energy and needing lots of movement. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "full of energy" still make sense? Yes, so you have it.
explain: Some energetic words are idioms, where the meaning is not the same as the separate words. «"Full of beans" means very energetic, almost hyperactive (UK).» A «live wire» is a very energetic child who cannot keep still, so you would not picture a real wire at all.
fact: Energetic means having lots of energy and being active and lively.
fact: Energetically is the adverb: she danced energetically means she danced with lots of energy.
fact: Energetic can describe a person, an animal or an activity.
fact: In science, energetic particles move faster.
fact: «Full of beans» (UK) and «live wire» both mean very energetic.
exercise: «Big, energetic dogs like huskies need lots of space and hours of running every day.» What does energetic mean here? | *Full of energy and needing lots of movement | Very small | Sleepy and calm | Old and tired
exercise: In PE, Mia says the game was energetic. What does she mean? | The game was played in a library | The game was about cooking | *The game needed lots of effort and running | The game was boring and still
exercise: Which phrase means very energetic? | Cold feet | Under the weather | *Full of beans | Off the top of my head
test: «She danced energetically at the party.» What does energetically tell you about the dancing? | Slowly and sadly | Without moving at all | Quietly, under her breath | *With lots of energy and effort
test: In «The Dodo says "I move that the meeting adjourn, for the immediate adoption of more energetic remedies"», what does energetic mean? | *More lively and active | More expensive | Written down | More tired
exam: Which sentence uses energetic correctly? | *The puppy chased the ball round the garden all afternoon, full of energy | The puppy slept on the sofa all day, so energetic that it never woke up
